==Serbo-Croatian==

===Etymology===
Literally “Spanish villages”, indicating an obscure field of knowledge.

A common misconception. "Španska sela" has nothing to do with Spain and its literall meaning isn't “Spanish villages”, as written earlier. Noun "Špan" is "Manager of manor (aristocrat) property".

